  "behavior": [
    "Unsigned full-word division and remainder accept bounded nonzero constant divisors, including high-bit divisors.",
    "Signed and unsigned 64-bit products preserve fixed-register operands, exact results, and overflow; signed 64-bit checked add/subtract preserve overflow.",
    "Full-word min/max and 16/32/64-bit byte swaps preserve live inputs and exact significant bits.",
    "The planner reserves scalar spill capacity across fixed-register arithmetic without eagerly relocating every ABI parameter.",
    "Private switch chains support zero and more than eight cases, 64-bit conditions, high unsigned i32 cases, duplicate PHI edges, and loops.",
    "The checked CFG bound supports through 1024 blocks with unchanged typed-action capacity.",
    "The unchanged pinned upstream Fibonacci program executes all six assertions in ReleaseFast and ReleaseSmall with LLVM-equivalent exit status, stdout and stderr."
  ],
